# ::tok http : / / www . ted . com / talks / ahn_trio_a_modern_take_on_piano_violin_cello< / url> <next_sent> Angella Ahn : Thank you . <next_sent> Thank you so much . <next_sent> We are so honored to be here at TEDWomen , sharing our music with you . <next_sent> What an exciting and inspiring event . <next_sent> What you just heard is " Skylife " by David Balakrishnan . <next_sent> We want to play you one more selection . <next_sent> It 's by Astor Piazzolla , an Argentine composer . <next_sent> And we talk about different ideas -- he had this idea that he thought music should be from the heart . <next_sent> This was in the middle of the 20th century when music from the heart , beautiful music , was n't the most popular thing in the classical music world . <next_sent> It was more atonal and twelve - tone . <next_sent> And he insisted on beautiful music . <next_sent> So this is " Oblivion " by Astor Piazzolla . <next_sent> Thank you .
